/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Smart Money Concepts \(SMC\) refer to the trading strategies and methodologies used by institutional investors, banks, and hedge funds. These entities, often referred to as "smart money," have the capital, resources, and market influence to move prices in a way that retail traders often cannot. Understanding SMC allows traders to align their strategies with institutional movements rather than being trapped in retail trading pitfalls.)
/E (Smart Money Concepts \(SMC\) refer to the trading strategies and methodologies used by institutional investors, banks, and hedge funds. These entities, often referred to as "smart money," have the capital, resources, and market influence to move prices in a way that retail traders often cannot. Understanding SMC allows traders to align their strategies with institutional movements rather than being trapped in retail trading pitfalls.)
/Pg 27 0 R
