1637 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Smart Money players, including large institutions and hedge funds, use their significant resources to manipulate liquidity, strategically enter and exit positions, and create market movements that often deceive retail traders. They achieve this by accumulating positions quietly, triggering false breakouts to grab liquidity, and then driving the market in their intended direction. Their actions can cause retail traders to enter poor positions or get stopped out before the real move occurs. Recognizing these patterns and understanding how Smart Money operates is crucial for traders who want to align with the market's true direction rather than being caught on the wrong side of a trade.)
/E (Smart Money players, including large institutions and hedge funds, use their significant resources to manipulate liquidity, strategically enter and exit positions, and create market movements that often deceive retail traders. They achieve this by accumulating positions quietly, triggering false breakouts to grab liquidity, and then driving the market in their intended direction. Their actions can cause retail traders to enter poor positions or get stopped out before the real move occurs. Recognizing these patterns and understanding how Smart Money operates is crucial for traders who want to align with the market's true direction rather than being caught on the wrong side of a trade.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
