/E ( Retail traders often dream of fast profits and try to achieve them by using excessive leverage or risking a large portion of their capital on a single trade. While this approach can produce quick wins, it also increases vulnerability to large losses. One wrong move can wipe out a substantial part of the trading account. Greed causes traders to ignore proper position sizing and risk management, eventually leading to blown accounts and emotional burnout.)
/Pg 29 0 R
