1773 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The first phase is the Accumulation Phase, where price moves sideways in a tight range with low volatility. During this period, institutions quietly build their positions while keeping the price stable. Retail traders often perceive this as mere consolidation, unaware that Smart Money is laying the groundwork for a larger move.)
/E (The first phase is the Accumulation Phase, where price moves sideways in a tight range with low volatility. During this period, institutions quietly build their positions while keeping the price stable. Retail traders often perceive this as mere consolidation, unaware that Smart Money is laying the groundwork for a larger move.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
1774 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Next comes the Manipulation Phase, also known as the liquidity grab. Here, a false breakout occurs to induce traders into poor positions, often triggering stop losses and collecting liquidity. Institutions use this phase to finalize their entries before initiating the real market move. Retail traders, misled by the fake breakout, find themselves trapped.)
/E (Next comes the Manipulation Phase, also known as the liquidity grab. Here, a false breakout occurs to induce traders into poor positions, often triggering stop losses and collecting liquidity. Institutions use this phase to finalize their entries before initiating the real market move. Retail traders, misled by the fake breakout, find themselves trapped.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
1775 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Finally, the Distribution Phase takes place, where the market moves aggressively in the intended direction after liquidity has been absorbed. This phase forces retail traders who were caught in bad positions to exit at a loss, while Smart Money traders take advantage of high-probability setups. As the market trends strongly, those who understood the cycle benefit from the predictable price movement.)
/E (Finally, the Distribution Phase takes place, where the market moves aggressively in the intended direction after liquidity has been absorbed. This phase forces retail traders who were caught in bad positions to exit at a loss, while Smart Money traders take advantage of high-probability setups. As the market trends strongly, those who understood the cycle benefit from the predictable price movement.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [7 8]
>>
