1837 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Risk management is essential when trading the AMD model. Set your stop-loss just below the liquidity grab \(for longs\) or above the fake breakout \(for shorts\). This prevents being stopped out unnecessarily while protecting capital. For take-profit targets, use previous liquidity zones, Fibonacci extensions, or a 1:2 to 1:3 risk-reward ratio. If the trade moves in your favor, consider taking partial profits at key levels and adjusting your stop-loss to breakeven to minimize risk.)
/E (Risk management is essential when trading the AMD model. Set your stop-loss just below the liquidity grab \(for longs\) or above the fake breakout \(for shorts\). This prevents being stopped out unnecessarily while protecting capital. For take-profit targets, use previous liquidity zones, Fibonacci extensions, or a 1:2 to 1:3 risk-reward ratio. If the trade moves in your favor, consider taking partial profits at key levels and adjusting your stop-loss to breakeven to minimize risk.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
