/P 5446 0 R
/E (High Liquidity: Markets with a high number of active buyers and sellers, leading to stable prices, smooth price action, and tight bid-ask spreads. These markets allow for large orders to be executed without significantly impacting the price. Examples include major forex pairs like EUR/USD, large-cap stocks such as Apple or Microsoft, and high-volume commodities like gold.)
/Pg 71 0 R
/K [8 9 10]
>>
endobj
2355 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 5447 0 R
/E (Low Liquidity: Markets with fewer participants, leading to increased price volatility, wider spreads, and difficulty executing large trades without causing price slippage. These conditions are commonly seen in exotic forex pairs \(e.g., USD/TRY\), low-volume stocks, and cryptocurrencies with small market capitalization.)
/Pg 71 0 R
/K [11 12]
>>
endobj
