/T (Buy-side liquidity refers to areas in the market where a significant number of buy orders exist. These often accumulate around key resistance levels or previous highs, where institutional traders execute large sell orders after inducing a liquidity grab. It includes buy-stop orders placed by traders shorting the market and new buy orders entered by breakout traders.)
/E (Buy-side liquidity refers to areas in the market where a significant number of buy orders exist. These often accumulate around key resistance levels or previous highs, where institutional traders execute large sell orders after inducing a liquidity grab. It includes buy-stop orders placed by traders shorting the market and new buy orders entered by breakout traders.)
