/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Think of Internal Range Liquidity as the stop losses hiding within the current price range. This range could be a sideways market \(consolidation\) or a swing move that hasn't broken the highs or lows yet. Retail traders often place their stops just above equal highs or below equal lows, expecting those levels to hold. But smart money sees these areas as easy targets.)
/E (Think of Internal Range Liquidity as the stop losses hiding within the current price range. This range could be a sideways market \(consolidation\) or a swing move that hasn't broken the highs or lows yet. Retail traders often place their stops just above equal highs or below equal lows, expecting those levels to hold. But smart money sees these areas as easy targets.)
/Pg 77 0 R
/K [5]
>>
