<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 5481 0 R
/E (Typically, these stop-losses are clustered above resistance levels and below support levels, forming what are known as liquidity zones. These areas become hotspots for institutional activity. When price approaches a swing high or low, institutions may deliberately push the price beyond these levels to trigger the pending stop-loss orders. This action creates a sudden influx of buy or sell orders, allowing institutions to absorb the resulting liquidity. By doing so, they can enter or exit positions with minimal slippage, often reversing the price soon after the liquidity has been captured.)
/Pg 79 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
