2487 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (For instance, if a stock is approaching a key resistance at $50, institutions may push the price slightly above that level, triggering a wave of retail buy orders. Once enough liquidity is generated, institutions place large sell orders, absorbing the influx of retail buying. This sudden shift in momentum causes the price to reverse quickly, dropping back below the breakout level. The result is a trap: retail traders find themselves caught in losing positions, their stop-losses triggered, while institutions exit profitably or enter in the opposite direction.)
/E (For instance, if a stock is approaching a key resistance at $50, institutions may push the price slightly above that level, triggering a wave of retail buy orders. Once enough liquidity is generated, institutions place large sell orders, absorbing the influx of retail buying. This sudden shift in momentum causes the price to reverse quickly, dropping back below the breakout level. The result is a trap: retail traders find themselves caught in losing positions, their stop-losses triggered, while institutions exit profitably or enter in the opposite direction.)
/Pg 80 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
