<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Institutions dominate the financial markets, using their size and resources to manipulate price action in ways that often catch retail traders off guard. Through tactics like stop-hunts, fake breakouts, liquidity sweeps, and order absorption, they create opportunities to enter and exit the market while leaving retail traders on the wrong side of the move. However, by understanding these strategies, retail traders can avoid common pitfalls and start trading in line with institutional intent.)
/Pg 85 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
