2561 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (One of the most common mistakes retail traders make is placing stop-losses too close to well-known support or resistance zones. These areas are heavily targeted by institutions looking to trigger stop orders and collect liquidity. Instead of placing stops at obvious levels, consider using structure-based exits or placing stop-losses beyond areas where stop-hunts are likely. This reduces the chance of getting taken out by a quick liquidity grab before the real move begins.)
/Pg 85 0 R
/K [13]
>>
