/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Liquidity zones are areas where price is likely to react due to a buildup of orders. These zones are often found at equal highs or lows, long wicks, or tight consolidation areas. Institutions frequently target these zones to execute large trades. By learning to spot these areas in advance, traders can be more cautious and avoid entering trades just before a sweep or reversal.)
/E (Liquidity zones are areas where price is likely to react due to a buildup of orders. These zones are often found at equal highs or lows, long wicks, or tight consolidation areas. Institutions frequently target these zones to execute large trades. By learning to spot these areas in advance, traders can be more cautious and avoid entering trades just before a sweep or reversal.)
