/T (In the chart below, we can see a clean example of equal highs being swept for liquidity. The market forms two swing highs at nearly the same level, creating a flat resistance zone that attracts retail attention. Most traders view this as a strong resistance area and either sell into it or place stop-losses just above. This behavior creates a build-up of buy-side liquidity above the highs.)
/E (In the chart below, we can see a clean example of equal highs being swept for liquidity. The market forms two swing highs at nearly the same level, creating a flat resistance zone that attracts retail attention. Most traders view this as a strong resistance area and either sell into it or place stop-losses just above. This behavior creates a build-up of buy-side liquidity above the highs.)
