3122 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Identifying high-probability order blocks is essential, but refining them ensures precision entries with minimal drawdown. Proper refinement helps traders reduce their stop-loss size, improve risk-to-reward ratios, and avoid false breakouts. Many traders enter trades blindly at order blocks without considering liquidity, market structure, or confirmation, which often leads to unnecessary losses. Refining order blocks helps filter out weak setups and focus only on those with institutional footprints.)
/Pg 123 0 R
/K [0]
>>
