/P 5556 0 R
/E (Bullish Order Block \(OB\): Most effective when it appears at a discount, which is below the 50% level of the most recent significant trading range \(measured from swing low to swing high\). This must occur within a bullish market structure, defined by higher highs \(HHs\) and higher lows \(HLs\). The idea is that institutional traders accumulate positions at discounted prices before initiating a strong upward move.)
/Pg 128 0 R
/K [4 5 6]
>>
endobj
3189 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 5557 0 R
/E (Bearish Order Block \(OB\): Most effective when it forms at a premium, which is above the 50% level of the range \(swing high to swing low\) during a bearish trend, characterized by lower highs \(LHs\) and lower lows \(LLs\). This suggests distribution by smart money at elevated prices before driving the market down.)
/Pg 128 0 R
/K [7 8]
>>
endobj
