/S /P
/E (When price enters the FVG zone, look for bullish confirmation before taking a trade. This confirmation could be in the form of bullish candlestick patterns like rejection wicks or engulfing candles, or other supporting signals such as confluence with an order block or a break in structure. These clues suggest that Smart Money may be defending the area and preparing for another upward move.)
/Pg 134 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
3278 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Once you see confirmation, consider entering a buy position either at the midpoint of the FVG or near the lower boundary of the gap. These entry levels are considered optimal because they offer better risk-to-reward and align with where unfilled buy orders are likely resting.)
/Pg 134 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
3279 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (               To manage risk, place your stop-loss just below the FVG. This protects you in case the market invalidates the gap or continues downward. For your take-profit, aim for logical targets such as the next area of liquidity, a recent swing high, or a resistance level where price is likely to react.)
/Pg 134 0 R
/K [7 8]
>>
