3353 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Fair Value Gaps reveal imbalance in the market. When price moves too quickly in one direction, it often skips over levels where normal buying and selling would occur. These gaps represent inefficiencies that the market often returns to "fill" before continuing.)
/Pg 139 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
3354 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E <>
/Pg 139 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
3355 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Inverse Fair Value Gaps \(iFVGs\) occur when price moves strongly in one direction, then quickly pulls back, breaks through that gap, and reverses. This kind of movement suggests the trend might be weakening, and a reversal could be coming. Traders watch these gaps closely because they can be early signs of the market changing direction.)
/Pg 139 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
