/E (1. Large Orders and Market Imbalances)
/Pg 140 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
3365 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Institutions rarely execute a single large order all at once. That would cause massive slippage, revealing their intentions to the market. Instead, they use execution algorithms to scale into or out of positions across multiple price levels. When Smart Money wants to buy, they aggressively lift offers, consuming liquidity and pushing price up before the retail crowd can react. The resulting gap in price action is a bullish Fair Value Gap. )
/Pg 140 0 R
/K [6 7]
>>
endobj
