/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (A Break of Structure \(BOS\) occurs when price breaks above a previous high \(in an uptrend\) or below a previous low \(in a downtrend\). This signals that the current trend is likely to continue. If a BOS happens close to an FVG, it strengthens the idea that price may retrace into the FVG and then continue in the direction of the trend, providing a high-probability entry point. \(See example below\))
/E (A Break of Structure \(BOS\) occurs when price breaks above a previous high \(in an uptrend\) or below a previous low \(in a downtrend\). This signals that the current trend is likely to continue. If a BOS happens close to an FVG, it strengthens the idea that price may retrace into the FVG and then continue in the direction of the trend, providing a high-probability entry point. \(See example below\))
/Pg 150 0 R
/K [2 3]
