/T (In Smart Money Concepts \(SMC\), we divide a price range into two main parts: the Premium Zone and the Discount Zone. The Premium Zone is the area above the 50% mark of a measured price swing, and it is considered "expensive." This is where traders typically look for selling opportunities, expecting the price to move lower. The Discount Zone is the area below the 50% mark, where the price is considered "cheap," making it ideal for buying opportunities, with the expectation that the price will rise. )
/E (In Smart Money Concepts \(SMC\), we divide a price range into two main parts: the Premium Zone and the Discount Zone. The Premium Zone is the area above the 50% mark of a measured price swing, and it is considered "expensive." This is where traders typically look for selling opportunities, expecting the price to move lower. The Discount Zone is the area below the 50% mark, where the price is considered "cheap," making it ideal for buying opportunities, with the expectation that the price will rise. )
