/T (The 50% level, known as Golden Ratio, acts as a basic guideline to tell us whether the market is priced at a premium \(good for selling\) or a discount \(good for buying\). However, the 50% line alone is not enough to guarantee accurate entries, because price often moves deeper into a range before reversing.To improve precision, we use Fibonacci retracement levels, especially the 61.8%, 71.5%, and 78.6% levels. These Fibonacci levels help us identify areas where professional traders and institutions are more likely to enter positions. )
/E (The 50% level, known as Golden Ratio, acts as a basic guideline to tell us whether the market is priced at a premium \(good for selling\) or a discount \(good for buying\). However, the 50% line alone is not enough to guarantee accurate entries, because price often moves deeper into a range before reversing.To improve precision, we use Fibonacci retracement levels, especially the 61.8%, 71.5%, and 78.6% levels. These Fibonacci levels help us identify areas where professional traders and institutions are more likely to enter positions. )
