/T (The first step is to find a clear and significant price move, either upward or downward. Look for a major Swing High, which is the highest point before the market starts falling, and a major Swing Low, which is the lowest point before the market starts rising. These swing points should be obvious and easy to spot, not small or random fluctuations. Once identified, mark these points clearly on your chart, as they will guide the next steps.)
/E (The first step is to find a clear and significant price move, either upward or downward. Look for a major Swing High, which is the highest point before the market starts falling, and a major Swing Low, which is the lowest point before the market starts rising. These swing points should be obvious and easy to spot, not small or random fluctuations. Once identified, mark these points clearly on your chart, as they will guide the next steps.)
