/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (When price experiences a strong upward move, it creates a clear Swing Low at the start of the move and a Swing High at the top. To analyze potential entry points during a pullback, you can apply the Fibonacci retracement tool from the Swing Low to the Swing High. This tool helps identify key levels where price might reverse before continuing its upward trend. The 50% retracement level divides the range into two zones. Below the 50% level lies the Discount Zone, where price is considered undervalued and more favorable for buying opportunities. Above the 50% level is the Premium Zone, where price is considered expensive and generally better suited for selling opportunities.)
/E (When price experiences a strong upward move, it creates a clear Swing Low at the start of the move and a Swing High at the top. To analyze potential entry points during a pullback, you can apply the Fibonacci retracement tool from the Swing Low to the Swing High. This tool helps identify key levels where price might reverse before continuing its upward trend. The 50% retracement level divides the range into two zones. Below the 50% level lies the Discount Zone, where price is considered undervalued and more favorable for buying opportunities. Above the 50% level is the Premium Zone, where price is considered expensive and generally better suited for selling opportunities.)
/Pg 162 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
3674 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (As a trader looking to buy during a pullback, the focus should be on entries within the Discount Zone, particularly near deeper Fibonacci retracement levels, which tend to offer higher-probability setups. The 61.8% retracement, known as the Golden Ratio, is one of the most respected levels in trading and often aligns with demand zones or bullish order blocks. The 78.6% retracement level represents an even deeper pullback and is frequently found near major liquidity pools, where institutional traders may step in. For example, if price pulls back to the 61.8% level and that level aligns with a well-defined demand order block, this creates a strong confluence that increases the likelihood of a bullish reversal. )
/E (As a trader looking to buy during a pullback, the focus should be on entries within the Discount Zone, particularly near deeper Fibonacci retracement levels, which tend to offer higher-probability setups. The 61.8% retracement, known as the Golden Ratio, is one of the most respected levels in trading and often aligns with demand zones or bullish order blocks. The 78.6% retracement level represents an even deeper pullback and is frequently found near major liquidity pools, where institutional traders may step in. For example, if price pulls back to the 61.8% level and that level aligns with a well-defined demand order block, this creates a strong confluence that increases the likelihood of a bullish reversal. )
/Pg 162 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
