/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (When price experiences a strong downward move, it forms a clear Swing High at the start of the move and a Swing Low at the bottom. To analyze potential entry points during a pullback \(retracement to the upside\), apply the Fibonacci retracement tool from the Swing High down to the Swing Low. This creates a range of key levels that help identify where the price may reverse and continue its downward trend. The 50% retracement level acts as the midpoint of the range and divides the price movement into two zones. Above the 50% level lies the Premium Zone, where price is considered expensive and more suitable for short \(sell\) opportunities. Below the 50% level is the Discount Zone, where price is relatively cheap, making it less favorable for initiating short positions.                      As a trader looking to sell in the Premium Zone, attention should be given to the deeper Fibonacci retracement levels, where higher-probability reversal setups often occur. )
/E (When price experiences a strong downward move, it forms a clear Swing High at the start of the move and a Swing Low at the bottom. To analyze potential entry points during a pullback \(retracement to the upside\), apply the Fibonacci retracement tool from the Swing High down to the Swing Low. This creates a range of key levels that help identify where the price may reverse and continue its downward trend. The 50% retracement level acts as the midpoint of the range and divides the price movement into two zones. Above the 50% level lies the Premium Zone, where price is considered expensive and more suitable for short \(sell\) opportunities. Below the 50% level is the Discount Zone, where price is relatively cheap, making it less favorable for initiating short positions.                      As a trader looking to sell in the Premium Zone, attention should be given to the deeper Fibonacci retracement levels, where higher-probability reversal setups often occur. )
/Pg 163 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
endobj
3685 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (For instance, if the price retraces to the 61.8% level and this aligns with a clear supply order block, this confluence increases the probability of a bearish reversal. In this scenario, a short position could be initiated near the 61.8% retracement level, ideally within or just below the order block. A well-placed stop-loss would go just above the 78.6% level to allow for normal market volatility while protecting against a deeper retracement that breaks structure. The ideal take-profit target would be the previous Swing Low, aiming to capture the full downside continuation from the retracement.                             This setup integrates market structure with Fibonacci logic and institutional activity, offering a calculated and risk-managed method for trading bearish pullbacks. By combining confluence zones, key retracement levels, and smart money behavior, traders can significantly improve the quality of their short entries.)
/E (For instance, if the price retraces to the 61.8% level and this aligns with a clear supply order block, this confluence increases the probability of a bearish reversal. In this scenario, a short position could be initiated near the 61.8% retracement level, ideally within or just below the order block. A well-placed stop-loss would go just above the 78.6% level to allow for normal market volatility while protecting against a deeper retracement that breaks structure. The ideal take-profit target would be the previous Swing Low, aiming to capture the full downside continuation from the retracement.                             This setup integrates market structure with Fibonacci logic and institutional activity, offering a calculated and risk-managed method for trading bearish pullbacks. By combining confluence zones, key retracement levels, and smart money behavior, traders can significantly improve the quality of their short entries.)
/Pg 163 0 R
/K [3]
>>
