3694 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The Optimal Trade Entry \(OTE\) strategy is a refined method used by institutional and smart money traders to enter trades with the highest possible reward-to-risk ratio and the least amount of drawdown. Rooted in Smart Money Concepts \(SMC\), OTE is designed to avoid emotional or early entries and instead focuses on precision. The strategy makes use of Fibonacci retracement levels to identify the most favorable price points where institutional activity is likely to occur. Rather than entering a trade at the first sign of a bounce from support or resistance, the OTE method encourages traders to wait for a deeper retracement into a high-probability zone before executing the trade.)
/Pg 164 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
