3762 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Before you take any trade, you need to know what the market is doing. Market structure is the way price moves over time, and it tells you whether the market is trending up, trending down, or moving sideways. This is important because trading with the trend gives you a much higher chance of success. In simple terms, the market moves in three ways: up, down, or sideways.)
/Pg 170 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
3763 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (An uptrend is when price keeps making higher highs \(HH\) and higher lows \(HL\). This means buyers are in control, and price is likely to keep rising. A downtrend is when price makes lower highs \(LH\) and lower lows \(LL\), showing that sellers are stronger and price may continue falling. If the price is not making new highs or new lows, and instead keeps bouncing between two levels, the market is said to be in a range or consolidation phase.)
/Pg 170 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
