/T (Liquidity zones often form above recent highs and below recent lows. These areas are known as Buy-Side Liquidity \(BSL\) and Sell-Side Liquidity \(SSL\). Buy-side liquidity exists above recent highs, where traders have placed stop-losses on short positions or pending buy orders. Sell-side liquidity is found below recent lows, where traders have stop-losses for long positions or pending sell orders.)
/E (Liquidity zones often form above recent highs and below recent lows. These areas are known as Buy-Side Liquidity \(BSL\) and Sell-Side Liquidity \(SSL\). Buy-side liquidity exists above recent highs, where traders have placed stop-losses on short positions or pending buy orders. Sell-side liquidity is found below recent lows, where traders have stop-losses for long positions or pending sell orders.)
