3912 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (After the liquidity sweep, look for a strong bullish move from the swept level. This shows the drop was just a liquidity grab. If the move breaks above the earlier bearish FVG, it turns into an inverse FVG \(iFVG\) and acts as support. This shift confirms buyers are in control and the uptrend is likely to continue. A new bullish Break of Structure \(BOS\) usually follows, signaling trend continuation. The iFVG or nearby Order Block \(OB\) often becomes a key area for price to retest. These zones offer high-probability entries for catching the next leg up.)
/E (After the liquidity sweep, look for a strong bullish move from the swept level. This shows the drop was just a liquidity grab. If the move breaks above the earlier bearish FVG, it turns into an inverse FVG \(iFVG\) and acts as support. This shift confirms buyers are in control and the uptrend is likely to continue. A new bullish Break of Structure \(BOS\) usually follows, signaling trend continuation. The iFVG or nearby Order Block \(OB\) often becomes a key area for price to retest. These zones offer high-probability entries for catching the next leg up.)
/Pg 181 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
