/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Once the range is established, the next move is to wait. Avoid trading within the range itself. Instead, allow price to break either above or below the range, effectively "sweeping" liquidity. This move is often fast and aggressive, designed to trigger stop orders and create a false sense of breakout. Most retail traders are caught during this phase, believing a new trend is starting. However, in reality, the market is setting up for a reversal.)
/E (Once the range is established, the next move is to wait. Avoid trading within the range itself. Instead, allow price to break either above or below the range, effectively "sweeping" liquidity. This move is often fast and aggressive, designed to trigger stop orders and create a false sense of breakout. Most retail traders are caught during this phase, believing a new trend is starting. However, in reality, the market is setting up for a reversal.)
/Pg 182 0 R
/K [7]
>>
